{
  "id": "guangzhou-master-tournament",
  "name": "Guangzhou Master Tournament",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Guangzhou Master Tournament (广州大师赛) of 2023 gave Simplified Chinese holo Rare Candy cards as prizes, stamped by result: a plain copy for players with five or more wins in the open division's preliminaries, or three or more in the senior and junior divisions; Top 64 for open-division players placed 9th to 64th; Top 8 for those placed 5th to 8th in any division; and Top 4, 2nd Place and Champion for the semi-finalists, runners-up and winners. Those top four players also got a Victory Decoration, the Simplified Chinese print of the trophy card of Japan's Champions League from 2017 to 2020.\n\nThe 2025 Guangzhou Master Tournament was held at the Poly World Trade Center Expo in Guangzhou on 5 and 6 April 2025. It was one of that year's four Master Tournaments (大师赛) in China, in Guangzhou, Hangzhou, Beijing and Shenzhen, whose prizes were Simplified Chinese holo Rare Candy cards stamped with the event and the player's result: a plain copy for a good record (the top 5,000 of the open division's preliminaries, seniors with four wins in their preliminaries and juniors with three wins in their breakthrough round), and Top 64, Top 8, 3rd Place, 2nd Place and Champion copies by final standing. The top finishers also got a Victory Symbol, the Simplified Chinese print of the trophy card of Japan's Champions League, stamped 3rd Place for those who finished third and fourth, 2nd Place or Champion.\n\nBuying designated card products at the tournament's shop came with a Zapdos ex with its logo. Every junior and senior entrant of the 2025 event, and every open-division player with priority entry to the main venue, got an event pack at check-in holding one of eight basic Energy cards with the tournament's logo.",
